# Check text out with LF everywhere, whatever core.autocrlf says.
#
# Not tidiness: a bin script's `#!/usr/bin/env node` line with a CR after it
# makes Linux and macOS look for a program called `node\r`, and npm publishes
# the working copy — so a release published from a default Windows checkout
# would ship commands that fail everywhere but Windows. scripts/release.js
# refuses to publish one; this stops it being created.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
*.tgz binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.db binary
